<title>USA: Teva gets FDA ok for calcium blocker.</title>
<headline>Teva gets FDA ok for calcium blocker.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Oct 29 (Reuter) Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd said Tuesday that it has received approval from the Food and Drug Administration to make and market Nicardipine capsules.</p>
<p>Teva said Nicardipine is a generic version of Cardene, a calcium channel blocker made by Roche Laboratories with about $20 million in annual sales.</p>
</text>
